-- title:
--   Norm-class index divides |Gal(E/k)| in 2-power degree
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ and $E$ be number fields with $E$ a Galois extension of $k$, suppose that the order $\mathrm{Nat.card}(E \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[k]} E)$ of the group of $k$-algebra automorphisms of $E$ equals $2^m$ for some natural number $m$, and let $\mathfrak{f}$ be an ideal of $\mathcal{O}_k$. Work inside `coprimeToModulus k 𝔣`, the subgroup of the unit group of fractional ideals of $k$ consisting of those $I$ whose valuation $\mathrm{count}_v(I)$ vanishes at every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_k$ dividing $\mathfrak{f}$. Two subgroups of it are formed by intersection: first, `narrowRaySubgroup k 𝔣`, the subgroup generated by the invertible fractional ideals of the form $(\alpha)$ with $\alpha \in \mathcal{O}_k$ nonzero, $\alpha - 1 \in \mathfrak{f}$ and $\tau(\alpha) > 0$ for every ring homomorphism $\tau : k \to \mathbb{R}$; second, the image of `coprimeToModulus E (𝔣.map (algebraMap (𝓞 k) (𝓞 E)))` under the homomorphism sending an invertible fractional ideal $J$ of $E$ to the finitely supported product $\prod_w \mathfrak{p}_{w \cap \mathcal{O}_k}^{\,f(w)\cdot \mathrm{count}_w(J)}$ over height-one primes $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_E$, where $\mathfrak{p}_{w\cap\mathcal{O}_k}$ is the fractional ideal attached to the prime of $\mathcal{O}_k$ under $w$ and $f(w)$ is the residue degree `inertiaDeg'` of $w$ over it, i.e.\ the relative ideal norm of $J$. The assertion is that the index of the join of these two subgroups in `coprimeToModulus k 𝔣` divides $\mathrm{Nat.card}(E \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[k]} E)$.
--
--   This is the ideal-theoretic second inequality of global class field theory, in divisibility form and at an arbitrary modulus, for Galois extensions whose group has $2$-power order: the group of ideals of $k$ prime to $\mathfrak{f}$, modulo the narrow ray group times the relative norms of ideals of $E$ prime to $\mathfrak{f}\mathcal{O}_E$, has order dividing the degree. It is obtained from the quadratic case [`M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_two`](thm.html#M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_two) by climbing a tower of quadratic steps via [`M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_mul_of_tower`](thm.html#M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_mul_of_tower), and is used in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the development to produce transfer data for Artin representations of small degree and to evaluate ray symbols on principal ideals.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aKummer_normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut.lean

import Definitions.Def_NarrowRayClassGroup

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open NumberField IsDedekindDomain Deep.NTSupply

theorem M4aKummer.normClassIndex_dvd_card_aut
    (k E : Type*) [Field k] [NumberField k] [Field E] [NumberField E] [Algebra k E] [IsGalois k E]
    (m : ℕ) (hm : Nat.card (E ≃ₐ[k] E) = 2 ^ m) (𝔣 : Ideal (𝓞 k)) :
    ((narrowRaySubgroup k 𝔣).subgroupOf (coprimeToModulus k 𝔣) ⊔
      ((coprimeToModulus E (𝔣.map (algebraMap (𝓞 k) (𝓞 E)))).map
        (raySymbolUnitsHom E (fun w : HeightOneSpectrum (𝓞 E) =>
          primeUnit k (w.under (𝓞 k)) ^ ((w.under (𝓞 k)).asIdeal.inertiaDeg' w.asIdeal)))).subgroupOf
        (coprimeToModulus k 𝔣)).index ∣ Nat.card (E ≃ₐ[k] E) := by sorry
